A||||12||William Federle||Starting problem||||1||
Z||000000||William Federle||07-02-2000||06:02 PM||||Help! I took my wife to the store after driving about 25 miles at freeway speeds and shut my car off. After waiting about 1/2 hour<BR>we got back in the car and it wouldn't turn over. <P>I checked to see if the clutch switch was loose - it looked ok.<P>The lights worked, the power windows worked, but the starter wouldn't turn over. <P>I pushed the car down a slight hill and had my wife pop the clutch in 2nd gear, but it wouldn't start. <P>Finally, I had my wife try to start it while I was in back, trying to hear if the solenoid was engaging. The car started.<P>Could it have been some sort of heat thing?<BR>The car didn't get over 190 while we were on our drive. This is the first time this has happened since I got the car last year. It has a new starter and solenoid.<P>I appreciate any advice.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||86SE||07-02-2000||06:12 PM||||Its probibly the starter solenoid.  I know if they get hot, sometimes they dont work until they cool down a bit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||William Federle||07-02-2000||06:15 PM||||Thanks - I've heard of people using some sort of heat-insulating tape. Maybe I'll try to find some of that and wrap the solenoid in it. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||07-02-2000||06:26 PM||||If it keeps happening you might want to replace the solenoid just to be safe.||||reg||14
Z||000004||William Federle||07-02-2000||06:37 PM||||Thanks. Have you heard of that insulating tape and if so do you know who carries it?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 07-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||07-02-2000||09:25 PM||||   Just went through this with my 85GT auto. It was the starter. I tried to replace the solenoid and was told that it is not sold as a seperate unit and wound up replacing the starter. Haven't had a problem since. They get old, they get hot, they don't work; it's that simple.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||William Federle||07-02-2000||11:05 PM||||Thanks for the tip. I got this thing from Autozone and I think they do sell solenoids separately for $9.00. If they don't I'll replace both.<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Taijiguy||07-03-2000||08:45 AM||||Doesn't Autozone have a lifetime warranty on that starter? I know they have one on just about everything else.||||reg||1
Z||000008||William Federle||07-03-2000||05:30 PM||||I thought about that but I couldn't find the receipt. I think this was a remanufactured unit but it's still under warrantee since it's been less than a year. The solenoid and a heat shield totaled about 12.50 including tax so I just got it. I guess I'll get a little more militant if it turns out not to be just the solenoid.<p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 07-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||86SE||07-03-2000||06:12 PM||||I just bought a starter with a lifetime warrenty for Advance Auto for a 4 banger for $39||||reg||14
Z||000010||ka4nkf||07-04-2000||08:35 AM||||It may be the starter solenoid, but I cant understand why It did not start when you pushed It and your wife poped the clutch. It should have started even If it didnt have a starter.||||reg||1
